What is adapted from it here, rewritten in Go (internal/controlplane/listening/x.go, issue #1291): X's web GraphQL
search, SearchTimeline, as a signed-in account (its variables, features, headers and the account's auth_token and ct0
cookies, lib/twitter-client-search.js, twitter-client-base.js, twitter-client-features.js), the parsing of its
timeline's posts and Bottom cursor (twitter-client-utils.js), its fallback query ids, and the reading of the query ids
from X's own JavaScript bundles (runtime-query-ids.js). The web client's bearer, which bird bakes in, is read from the
same bundles instead.

